# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Claude / Codex / assistant memory
.claude
superpowers
.superpowers
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
# Working artifacts (specs, mockups) stay local.
# Allowlist operator-facing runbooks + multi-agent handoff plans.
# Plan files are created per-feature under docs/plans/ and deleted on merge.
/docs/*
!/docs/operator/
!/docs/operator/**
!/docs/architecture.md
!/docs/security.md

# Git worktrees (isolated workspaces for feature branches)
.worktrees/

# Build artifacts
bin/
/schlass
internal/web/dist/*
!internal/web/dist/.gitkeep

# Environment
.env

# Dependencies
web/node_modules/

# Playwright artifacts
web/playwright-report/
web/test-results/

# Manual UAT scaffolding — local-only third-party RP compose files,
# baked-in client credentials, not part of the shipping artifact.
# Walkthrough lives in docs/operator/oidc-rp-integration.md.
/uat/
.codex

# Local milestone tracker on long-lived feature branches. Never travels
# to main on squash-merge — subagents read + update it during work.
internal/audit/MILESTONE.md
internal/audit/CRITICAL_PROPAGATION.md
